#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:107
msgid ""
"Multiplying a string by an integer repeats it, so ``\"ab\" * 3`` produces "
"the string concatenated three times: ``ababab``."
msgstr ""
"Multiplicar una cadena por un entero la repite, así que ``\"ab\" * 3`` "
"produce la cadena concatenada tres veces: ``ababab``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:124
msgid "``[0, 3]``"
msgstr "``[0, 3]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:125
msgid "``[0, 0, 0]``"
msgstr "``[0, 0, 0]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:126
msgid "``[[0], [0], [0]]``"
msgstr "``[[0], [0], [0]]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:127
msgid "``[3]``"
msgstr "``[3]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:132
msgid ""
"The ``*`` operator on a list repeats its elements, so ``[0] * 3`` builds a "
"new list containing the single element three times: ``[0, 0, 0]``."
msgstr ""
"El operador ``*`` sobre una lista repite sus elementos, así que ``[0] * 3`` "
"construye una nueva lista que contiene el único elemento tres veces: ``[0, "
"0, 0]``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:149
msgid "``on``"
msgstr "``on``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:150
msgid "``ho``"
msgstr "``ho``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:151 ../../../syntax-easy.rst:175
msgid "``yth``"
msgstr "``yth``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:152
msgid "``n``"
msgstr "``n``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:157
msgid ""
"Index ``-2`` is the second-to-last character (``o``), and the open-ended "
"slice ``[-2:]`` runs from there to the end, giving ``on``."
msgstr ""
"El índice ``-2`` es el penúltimo carácter (``o``), y el corte abierto "
"``[-2:]`` va desde ahí hasta el final, dando ``on``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:174
msgid "``pyt``"
msgstr "``pyt``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:176
msgid "``ytho``"
msgstr "``ytho``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:177
msgid "``python``"
msgstr "``python``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:182
msgid ""
"Slicing is half-open: ``[1:4]`` includes indexes 1, 2 and 3 but stops before"
" index 4, so from ``\"python\"`` you get ``yth``."
msgstr ""
"El corte es semiabierto: ``[1:4]`` incluye los índices 1, 2 y 3 pero se "
"detiene antes del índice 4, así que de ``\"python\"`` obtienes ``yth``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:199
msgid "``<class 'int'>``"
msgstr "``<class 'int'>``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:200
msgid "``<class 'tuple'>``"
msgstr "``<class 'tuple'>``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:201
msgid "``<class 'list'>``"
msgstr "``<class 'list'>``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:202
msgid "``<class 'set'>``"
msgstr "``<class 'set'>``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:207
msgid ""
"It is the trailing comma, not the parentheses, that makes a tuple. ``(1,)`` "
"is a one-element tuple, whereas ``(1)`` would just be the integer ``1``."
msgstr ""
"Es la coma final, no los paréntesis, lo que crea una tupla. ``(1,)`` es una "
"tupla de un elemento, mientras que ``(1)`` sería simplemente el entero "
"``1``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:225 ../../../syntax-easy.rst:426
msgid "``0``"
msgstr "``0``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:227
msgid "``3.33``"
msgstr "``3.33``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:232
msgid ""
"``%`` is the modulo (remainder) operator. ``10`` divided by ``3`` is ``3`` "
"with a remainder of ``1``, so the result is ``1``."
msgstr ""
"``%`` es el operador módulo (resto). ``10`` dividido entre ``3`` da ``3`` "
"con un resto de ``1``, así que el resultado es ``1``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:250
msgid "``7``"
msgstr "``7``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:252
msgid "``123``"
msgstr "``123``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:257
msgid ""
"Multiplication has higher precedence than addition, so ``2 * 3`` is "
"evaluated first, then ``1 +`` is added, giving ``7``."
msgstr ""
"La multiplicación tiene mayor precedencia que la suma, así que ``2 * 3`` se "
"evalúa primero, luego se suma ``1 +``, dando ``7``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:275 ../../../syntax-easy.rst:403
#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:428
msgid "``True``"
msgstr "``True``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:282
msgid ""
"``bool`` is a subclass of ``int``, where ``True`` equals ``1``. Adding them "
"with ``+`` does integer arithmetic, so ``True + True`` is ``2``."
msgstr ""
"``bool`` es una subclase de ``int``, donde ``True`` equivale a ``1``. "
"Sumarlos con ``+`` hace aritmética entera, así que ``True + True`` es ``2``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:299
msgid "``abab``"
msgstr "``abab``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:300
msgid "``abb``"
msgstr "``abb``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:301
msgid "``aab``"
msgstr "``aab``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:302
msgid "``ab2``"
msgstr "``ab2``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:307
msgid ""
"``*`` binds tighter than ``+``, so ``\"b\" * 2`` (``\"bb\"``) is computed "
"first, then concatenated after ``\"a\"``, giving ``abb``."
msgstr ""
"``*`` liga con más fuerza que ``+``, así que ``\"b\" * 2`` (``\"bb\"``) se "
"calcula primero, luego se concatena tras ``\"a\"``, dando ``abb``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:324
msgid "``abc``"
msgstr "``abc``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:325
msgid "``ace``"
msgstr "``ace``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:326
msgid "``bdf``"
msgstr "``bdf``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:327
msgid "``fedcba``"
msgstr "``fedcba``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:332
msgid ""
"The third slice value is the step. ``[::2]`` starts at the beginning and "
"takes every second character, so from ``\"abcdef\"`` you get ``ace``."
msgstr ""
"El tercer valor del corte es el paso. ``[::2]`` empieza al principio y toma "
"un carácter de cada dos, así que de ``\"abcdef\"`` obtienes ``ace``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:350
msgid "``5 5``"
msgstr "``5 5``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:351
msgid "``5``"
msgstr "``5``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:352
msgid "``5 None``"
msgstr "``5 None``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:353
msgid "``NameError``"
msgstr "``NameError``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:358
msgid ""
"Chained assignment binds the same value to every target, so both ``a`` and "
"``b`` become ``5`` and the line prints ``5 5``."
msgstr ""
"La asignación encadenada asigna el mismo valor a cada destino, así que tanto"
" ``a`` como ``b`` se convierten en ``5`` y la línea imprime ``5 5``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:376
msgid "``12``"
msgstr "``12``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:378
msgid "``(1, 2)``"
msgstr "``(1, 2)``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:384
msgid ""
"Tuple unpacking assigns ``a = 1`` and ``b = 2``, so ``a + b`` is the integer"
" sum ``3``."
msgstr ""
"El desempaquetado de tuplas asigna ``a = 1`` y ``b = 2``, así que ``a + b`` "
"es la suma entera ``3``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:401
msgid "``yes``"
msgstr "``yes``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:402
msgid "``no``"
msgstr "``no``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:404 ../../../syntax-easy.rst:479
msgid "``SyntaxError``"
msgstr "``SyntaxError``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:409
msgid ""
"This is a conditional expression: the value before ``if`` is used when the "
"condition is true. Since ``5 > 3`` is true, it evaluates to ``yes``."
msgstr ""
"Esto es una expresión condicional: el valor antes de ``if`` se usa cuando la"
" condición es verdadera. Como ``5 > 3`` es verdadero, se evalúa a ``yes``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:427
msgid "``hi``"
msgstr "``hi``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:429
msgid "``False``"
msgstr "``False``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:434
msgid ""
"``or`` returns the first truthy operand (or the last one). ``0`` is falsy, "
"so it returns the second operand, the string ``hi`` itself, not a boolean."
msgstr ""
"``or`` devuelve el primer operando verdadero (o el último). ``0`` es falso, "
"así que devuelve el segundo operando, la propia cadena ``hi``, no un "
"booleano."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:451
msgid "``[0, 1, 2]``"
msgstr "``[0, 1, 2]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:452
msgid "``[0, 2, 4]``"
msgstr "``[0, 2, 4]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:453
msgid "``[2, 4, 6]``"
msgstr "``[2, 4, 6]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:454
msgid "``[0, 2, 4, 6]``"
msgstr "``[0, 2, 4, 6]``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:459
msgid ""
"``range(3)`` yields ``0, 1, 2`` and the comprehension doubles each, "
"producing ``[0, 2, 4]``."
msgstr ""
"``range(3)`` genera ``0, 1, 2`` y la comprensión duplica cada uno, "
"produciendo ``[0, 2, 4]``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:476
msgid "``1_000_000``"
msgstr "``1_000_000``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:477
msgid "``1000000``"
msgstr "``1000000``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:478
msgid "``1000``"
msgstr "``1000``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:484
msgid ""
"Underscores are legal digit-group separators in numeric literals; they are "
"purely cosmetic, so ``1_000_000`` is just the integer ``1000000``."
msgstr ""
"Los guiones bajos son separadores de grupos de dígitos válidos en los "
"literales numéricos; son puramente estéticos, así que ``1_000_000`` es "
"simplemente el entero ``1000000``."

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:501
msgid "``0xff``"
msgstr "``0xff``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:502
msgid "``255``"
msgstr "``255``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:503
msgid "``16``"
msgstr "``16``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:504
msgid "``15``"
msgstr "``15``"

#: ../../../syntax-easy.rst:509
msgid ""
"The ``0x`` prefix marks a hexadecimal literal. ``ff`` in base 16 is ``15 * "
"16 + 15``, which prints as the decimal integer ``255``."
msgstr ""
"El prefijo ``0x`` marca un literal hexadecimal. ``ff`` en base 16 es ``15 * "
"16 + 15``, que se imprime como el entero decimal ``255``."
